.th PAGE I APR/79
.sh NAME
page \*- flexible pagination of output
.sh SYNOPSIS
.bd page
[ \fB-nnn\fR ]
file ...
.sh DESCRIPTION
.it page
reads from its input, breaking on 22 line pages.
If no files are given then the standard
input is read.
Between pages it reads a carriage return
from the terminal in no echo. If delete is hit while printing
a file, then
.it page
silently expires.
The page-length can be set with the \fB-\fR flag.
.i0
.dt
.sh AUTHOR
Adrian Freed (AGSM)
.sh BUGS
It could do more, but at least this one works!
